Model narration for stages 1-5 unchanged. Now stage6-nodes.js (DOM injection), render.js, render-stage.js, inspector-source-stage6.js, inspector-state.js, panel.js.

stage6-nodes.js design:

```js
// DOCUMENTS: Stage 6 DOM injection — the panel page sits at its 550-line
// cap (guard-file-size), so the two Stage 6 node cards, their inspector
// tabs, and the live stage-pill-6 are built here with createElement only
// (textContent/attributes — no inline styles, no innerHTML, CSP-safe) and
// appended before panel.js wires its listeners.

export function initStage6Nodes() {
  // stage-pill-6: replace the static "6 · Multi-Net / CDN" placeholder span
  const ladder = document.querySelector('.stage-ladder');
  const placeholder = [...ladder.querySelectorAll('.stage-pill')].find((el) => el.textContent.includes('6 ·'));
  const pill = document.createElement('button');
  pill.type = 'button';
  pill.className = 'stage-pill';
  pill.dataset.testid = 'stage-pill-6';
  pill.dataset.stage = '6';
  pill.title = 'Switch to Stage 6 — DNS and cross-subnet routing';
  pill.textContent = '6 · Multi-Net / CDN';
  placeholder.replaceWith(pill);
```

Wait — does the title attribute matter? "Give every trace, camera, and load control a non-empty title" — stage pills don't have titles... other pills don't. The e2e title test checks specific ids only. A title is harmless but inconsistent; skip it? DESIGN says every trace/camera/load control — stage pills not included. Skip title for consistency with pills 1-5.

